Thickness of aquifer, $H=20 \mathrm{~m}$

$$\begin{aligned}

& r_{1}=10 \mathrm{~m} \\

& r_{2}=100 \mathrm{~m} \\

& h_{2}=H-S_{w 1}=20-5=15 \mathrm{~m} \\

& h_{1}=H-S_{w 2}=20-1=19 \mathrm{~m}

\end{aligned}$$

Now discharge for unconfined aquifer is given as

$$\begin{aligned}

& Q=\frac{\pi \cdot K\left[h_{1}^{2}-h_{2}^{2}\right]}{\ln \left[\frac{r_{2}}{r_{1}}\right]}=\frac{\pi \times 10 \times\left[19^{2}-15^{2}\right]}{\ln \left[\frac{100}{10}\right]} \\

& Q=1855.55 \mathrm{~m}^{3} / \text { day }

\end{aligned}$$

Therefore, the correct answer is **1855** (acceptable range: [1852, 1858]).
